// Vectors from the C# reference, M0LTE.Ms110d 0.3.0 (the NuGet package pinned in
// reference/pin.txt). Generated by tools/csharp-vectors (Program.cs prints them,
// make_header.py formats them); it calls only public types:
//   Ms110dScrambler.NextPsk / NextQam, Trinomial159Scrambler.Next, Ms110dInterleaver and
//   Ms110dInterleaverParams.Get3k / Has3k (the sizes and
//   increments themselves are in tests/data/csharp-tables-0.3.0.txt, see TablesDump.cs).
// Hashes are 64-bit FNV-1a over each value as a 32-bit little-endian word. Scrambler lists
// are the first outputs from a fresh register with input symbol 0 ("head"), and the hash of
// 1024 outputs (4200 for the trinomial); "mix" feeds the input symbol i % 8 (PSK) or
// i & (2^bits - 1) (QAM) instead. Interleaver rows come from the C# parameter table and give
// the first 16 load locations (the wire position of bit n, extracted by interleaving the
// indices 0..size-1 and inverting) and the hash of all of them, plus the hash of the
// fetched array when input byte i is (i & 255).
// Do not edit by hand; regenerate from the C# if the pin moves.

